{ ==========================================================================
  IND_S16S_CONV6  --  the six convergence patterns, as a subchart ribbon

  Build_ID 260901.  DETECTION ONLY.  Places no orders, holds no position.

  P01 NR4 / P02 NR7 / P03 inside x2 / P04 inside x3 / P05 ID-NR4
  / P06 three shrinking ranges

  WHY A SEPARATE INDICATOR, AND WHY A RIBBON

    Ruling of 2026-08-31: draw all six, but present them concisely.

    Measured first, because the answer follows from the number.  The six
    together mark 148,748 bars -- 35.29% of the series, one every 2.8 --
    which is 104 marks on a median 300-bar screen and 145 at the worst.
    Today's seven pivot shapes are 26 and 58 for comparison.

    At that density TEXT IS THE WRONG PRIMITIVE.  A label reading
    "P01 #135778" is about ten characters wide; one every 2.8 bars means
    they overlap horizontally no matter which lane they sit in, because the
    collision is in width, not in height.  Lanes solved the seven; they
    cannot solve this.

    So each mark is exactly one bar wide and lives in its own row.  Six
    rows, rarest at the top, densest at the bottom -- the same ordering the
    label lanes use in IND_S16S_P29.  A dense row reads as a band, which is
    information (it shows where compression clusters), and it cannot
    trespass on another pattern's row.

    Separate file because these six paint nothing on price.  Putting them
    in IND_S16S_P29 would have them competing with the pattern bodies that
    file already recolours.

  THE ROWS, bottom to top

    1  P01 NR4            135,778   every 3.1 bars
    2  P02 NR7             89,164   every 4.7
    3  P06 3 shrinking     63,022   every 6.7
    4  P05 ID-NR4          57,140   every 7.4
    5  P03 inside x2       12,730   every 33.1
    6  P04 inside x3        1,784   every 236.3

  NO GAPS, ON PURPOSE

    Every row plots on EVERY bar.  Firing is carried by COLOUR, not by
    whether the plot exists.  On 2026-08-26 a NoPlot-gapped plot in
    IND_S16S_P29 drew lines spanning the whole chart, because MC12
    interpolates across the gap.  A plot that never gaps cannot do that.
    Off-bars take Col_Idle, which should be left close to the chart
    background.

  SESSION RULE -- the reason this is not optional

    These six read ADJACENT BARS, not pivots, so every one of them is
    adjacency-dependent and none may span a session break.  Measured cost
    of leaving it out: P02 3,124 false fires (3.39%), P01 1,785, P05 825,
    P06 328, P03 31, P04 10.  Same failure as the twelve two-bar patterns
    on 2026-08-21.

  FREE PARAMETERS

    N = 4 and N = 7 are Crabel's constants and have no geometric
    derivation.  Accepted by ruling on 2026-08-31 -- recorded here as
    borrowed, not derived, so nobody later mistakes them for the latter.
    P03, P04 and P06 carry none.

    "Narrowest" counts ties (<=), matching the inside-bar test, which is
    non-strict because the previous bar's range IS the band and a
    non-strict inside bar is exactly the band device of the 2026-08-29
    ruling.  For NR there is no such derivation, so ties are a CHOICE and
    still awaiting a ruling; the strict alternative costs 31.8% of P01 and
    41.7% of P02.

  ACCEPTANCE, printed on the last bar as CONV6 TALLY
    bars 421,507
    P01 135777   P02 89163   P03 12730   P04 1784   P05 57140   P06 63021
    VERIFIED in MC12 on 2026-08-31, all six plus the bar count.

    Those are the full csv (421,513 bars) MINUS THIS FILE'S OWN WARM-UP.
    v_NBars counts from CurrentBar 1, which MC12 places after the deepest
    bar reference the file makes -- High[6] here, so six bars.  The full-csv
    figures are 135778 / 89164 / 12730 / 1784 / 57140 / 63022.

    NOTE: two indicators on the SAME chart report different bars=.
    IND_S16S_P29 reports 421,455 on this chart, 58 short, and that was
    written up on 2026-08-31 as the chart having loaded fewer bars.  It had
    not: CONV6 sees 421,507 on the same chart, so the data is complete and
    the 58 is P29's warm-up.  A property of the code, described as a
    property of the data -- the same mistake as the diamond index bug
    earlier the same day.  Read bars= as "this file's warm-up", never as
    "the chart's length".

  HOW TO SET IT UP
    Apply to a SUBCHART, not the price pane.
    Style tab: set every plot to Point or a thick line.  Scaling tab:
    set the range to 0 .. 7 so the six rows sit evenly.
  ======================================================================== }

inputs:
    Build_ID                ( 260901 ),
    Sess_Day_Start          ( 845   ),
    Sess_Day_End            ( 1345  ),
    Sess_Night_Start        ( 1500  ),
    Sess_Night_End          ( 500   ),
    Enable_P01              ( 1     ),     { NR4, 135,778 }
    Enable_P02              ( 1     ),     { NR7, 89,164 }
    Enable_P03              ( 1     ),     { inside x2, 12,730 }
    Enable_P04              ( 1     ),     { inside x3, 1,784 }
    Enable_P05              ( 1     ),     { ID-NR4, 57,140 }
    Enable_P06              ( 1     ),     { three shrinking, 63,022 }
    Col_P01                 ( DarkGray  ),
    Col_P02                 ( Blue      ),
    Col_P03                 ( Cyan      ),
    Col_P04                 ( Magenta   ),
    Col_P05                 ( DarkGreen ),
    Col_P06                 ( DarkRed   ),
    Col_Idle                ( Black     ),  { leave near the background }
    Print_Events            ( 0     );

variables:
    v_In_Day                ( False ),
    v_In_Night              ( False ),
    v_In_Sess               ( False ),
    v_Sess_First            ( False ),
    v_BIS                   ( 0     ),     { bars into the session }
    v_R                     ( 0     ),
    v_Ins0                  ( False ),
    v_Ins1                  ( False ),
    v_Ins2                  ( False ),
    v_NR4                   ( False ),
    v_NR7                   ( False ),
    v_H1                    ( False ),
    v_H2                    ( False ),
    v_H3                    ( False ),
    v_H4                    ( False ),
    v_H5                    ( False ),
    v_H6                    ( False ),
    v_C01                   ( 0     ),
    v_C02                   ( 0     ),
    v_C03                   ( 0     ),
    v_C04                   ( 0     ),
    v_C05                   ( 0     ),
    v_C06                   ( 0     ),
    v_NBars                 ( 0     ),
    v_Ymd                   ( 0     );

    { ---------- SESSION.  Same construction as IND_S16S_P29 SECTION 1,
      deliberately -- a second implementation of the session counter is
      how two files start disagreeing. ---------- }

v_In_Day   = Time >  Sess_Day_Start   and Time <= Sess_Day_End;
v_In_Night = Time >  Sess_Night_Start or  Time <= Sess_Night_End;
v_In_Sess  = v_In_Day or v_In_Night;

v_Sess_First = False;
if CurrentBar > 1 then begin
    if v_In_Day   and ( v_In_Day[1]   = False ) then v_Sess_First = True;
    if v_In_Night and ( v_In_Night[1] = False ) then v_Sess_First = True;
end;

if v_Sess_First then
    v_BIS = 1
else if v_In_Sess then
    v_BIS = v_BIS + 1
else
    v_BIS = 0;

v_NBars = v_NBars + 1;

    { ---------- THE SIX.  Every one needs v_BIS >= its own bar count. --- }

v_R = High - Low;

{ inside bar: the previous bar's range IS the band, and the test is
  non-strict because that is what the band device says -- 83.3% of P03 and
  95.6% of P04 turn on this one choice. }
v_Ins0 = ( High     <= High[1] ) and ( Low     >= Low[1] );
v_Ins1 = ( High[1]  <= High[2] ) and ( Low[1]  >= Low[2] );
v_Ins2 = ( High[2]  <= High[3] ) and ( Low[2]  >= Low[3] );

v_NR4 = v_R <= MinList( High[1] - Low[1], High[2] - Low[2],
                        High[3] - Low[3] );
v_NR7 = v_NR4
        and v_R <= MinList( High[4] - Low[4], High[5] - Low[5],
                            High[6] - Low[6] );

v_H1 = Enable_P01 <> 0 and v_BIS >= 4 and v_NR4;
v_H2 = Enable_P02 <> 0 and v_BIS >= 7 and v_NR7;
v_H3 = Enable_P03 <> 0 and v_BIS >= 3 and v_Ins0 and v_Ins1;
v_H4 = Enable_P04 <> 0 and v_BIS >= 4 and v_Ins0 and v_Ins1 and v_Ins2;
v_H5 = Enable_P05 <> 0 and v_BIS >= 4 and v_NR4 and v_Ins0;
v_H6 = Enable_P06 <> 0 and v_BIS >= 3
       and v_R < High[1] - Low[1]
       and High[1] - Low[1] < High[2] - Low[2];

if v_H1 then v_C01 = v_C01 + 1;
if v_H2 then v_C02 = v_C02 + 1;
if v_H3 then v_C03 = v_C03 + 1;
if v_H4 then v_C04 = v_C04 + 1;
if v_H5 then v_C05 = v_C05 + 1;
if v_H6 then v_C06 = v_C06 + 1;

    { ---------- THE RIBBON.  Rarest on top, densest at the bottom, the
      same ordering the label lanes use.  Every row plots on every bar so
      there is no gap for MC12 to interpolate across. ---------- }

Plot1( 1, "NR4" );
Plot2( 2, "NR7" );
Plot3( 3, "Shrink3" );
Plot4( 4, "ID-NR4" );
Plot5( 5, "Inside2" );
Plot6( 6, "Inside3" );

if v_H1 then SetPlotColor( 1, Col_P01 ) else SetPlotColor( 1, Col_Idle );
if v_H2 then SetPlotColor( 2, Col_P02 ) else SetPlotColor( 2, Col_Idle );
if v_H6 then SetPlotColor( 3, Col_P06 ) else SetPlotColor( 3, Col_Idle );
if v_H5 then SetPlotColor( 4, Col_P05 ) else SetPlotColor( 4, Col_Idle );
if v_H3 then SetPlotColor( 5, Col_P03 ) else SetPlotColor( 5, Col_Idle );
if v_H4 then SetPlotColor( 6, Col_P04 ) else SetPlotColor( 6, Col_Idle );

if Print_Events <> 0 and ( v_H3 or v_H4 ) then begin
    v_Ymd = Date + 19000000;
    Print( "CONV6 INSIDE ", v_Ymd:8:0, " ", Time:4:0,
           "  x2=", v_C03:6:0, "  x3=", v_C04:6:0 );
end;

if CurrentBar = 1 then Print( "IND_S16S_CONV6 build ", Build_ID:6:0 );

if LastBarOnChart then begin
    Print( "CONV6 DIAG   bars=", v_NBars:8:0,
           "  last=", ( Date + 19000000 ):8:0, " ", Time:4:0 );
    Print( "CONV6 TALLY  P01=", v_C01:7:0, "  P02=", v_C02:7:0,
           "  P03=", v_C03:6:0, "  P04=", v_C04:5:0,
           "  P05=", v_C05:7:0, "  P06=", v_C06:7:0 );
    Print( "CONV6 TALLY  reference   135777    89163   12730   1784",
           "    57140    63021   (after this file 6-bar warm-up)" );
end;
